---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AuthorByline from '../components/AuthorByline.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is spf record syntax in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="SPF Record Syntax: Every Mechanism and Qualifier" description="Complete SPF syntax reference: every mechanism (include, ip4, ip6, a, mx, exists), every qualifier, modifiers, and evaluation order."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">SPF Syntax</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">SPF Syntax: The Complete Reference</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      An SPF record is one TXT string, evaluated left to right, first match wins. Every term is a
      qualifier glued to a mechanism, plus a couple of modifiers. This is every piece of that grammar.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
      <table class="pdns-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Kind</th><th>Lookup?</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">v=spf1</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">version</td><td class="text-xs">no</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Required first token.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">ip4:1.2.3.4</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">no</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches that IPv4 (CIDR ranges allowed).</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">ip6:...</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">no</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches an IPv6 address or range.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">a / a:domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches the domain's A/AAAA records.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">mx / mx:domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches the domain's MX hosts' addresses.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">include:domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Evaluates another domain's SPF; a pass there is a pass here.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">exists:domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches if the name resolves at all (rare, macro use).</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">ptr / ptr:domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">0</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Deprecated reverse-DNS match; remove it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">all</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">mechanism</td><td class="text-xs">no</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Matches everything; its qualifier sets the default verdict.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">redirect=domain</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">modifier</td><td class="text-xs">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Replace evaluation with another domain's record.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">exp=text</td><td class="text-xs text-ink-faint">modifier</td><td class="text-xs">no</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Explanation string for failures; rarely used.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>The qualifiers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>+</code> pass (default when no qualifier is written)</li>
        <li><code>-</code> hard fail: receivers should reject</li>
        <li><code>~</code> soft fail: accept but penalize; the common safe default on <code>~all</code></li>
        <li><code>?</code> neutral: no assertion either way</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Evaluation in one paragraph</h2>
      <p>
        The receiver walks terms left to right against the connecting IP. First mechanism that matches
        returns its qualifier's verdict and evaluation stops. If nothing matches, <code>all</code>
        catches the remainder, which is why your terminal qualifier defines your posture. Every
        include/a/mx/exists/redirect costs one of the
        <a href="/spf-lookup-limit/">10 permitted lookups</a>; exceeding them returns permerror, a
        broken record. Test any change with the <a href="/spf-record-checker/">SPF checker</a>.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is spf record syntax in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/spf-record/">SPF: the complete guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/spf-flattener/">SPF flattener</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <AuthorByline />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
